# The site needs no environment variables.
#
# That is not an omission — it is the architecture. Every page is prerendered to
# static HTML at build time, and the market and chain data it shows is read in
# the visitor's own browser from public, keyless, CORS-open APIs. There is no
# server, no database and no account to hold a credential for, so there is
# nothing here that could leak and nothing you have to be given before you can
# run it.
#
#   git clone --depth 1 <repo> && npm install && npm run dev
#
# is the whole setup. If you copied this file to `.env` expecting to fill
# something in: you do not need to.
#
# `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored, with this file the one exception. If a
# feature ever does need a secret, it goes in the environment of the host that
# runs it — never in the repository, and never behind a PUBLIC_ prefix, which
# would ship it to the browser.
#
# See the Security section of the README for what the site does hold, which is
# nothing, and why.
